"""{{ project_name }} — {{ description }}

The package is laid out by domain rather than by layer: everything about users
lives under ``app.modules.users``, everything about items under
``app.modules.items``, and each module has the same five files. Finding the code
for a feature means opening one directory, and deleting a feature means deleting
one directory.

The layers inside a module are strictly ordered, and the order is the whole
point:

    router  ->  service  ->  repository  ->  models
      HTTP      business      queries       tables
                  logic

A router knows about HTTP and calls services. A service opens a transaction and
returns Pydantic schemas. A repository takes a session and runs queries. Nothing
points back up.
